   "evidence": "`grep -rn 'LightFlavor' EpsilonEridani` matches only `Particles/Meson/Basic.lean` and the new `DIS/Inclusive/Isospin.lean`; `Meson/Basic.lean:293` `inductive LightFlavor`, `:317` `noncomputable def charge : LightFlavor \u2192 \u211d`. The roadmap places flavour-indexed density material under `EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/` (README.md:94), not under `Meson/`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Inclusive/Isospin.lean",
   "fix": "Mechanically `git mv` `LightFlavor`, its `Fintype` instance, `sum_univ`, `charge` and `charge_u/d/s` (`Particles/Meson/Basic.lean:292-328`) into a flavour-level module, e.g. `EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/Flavor.lean` next to `Parton/Species.lean`, which also indexes quark flavours; have `Meson/Basic.lean` and this file import that module instead. No declaration renames are needed. If this is judged too large for one topic, ship it as a prerequisite PR and rebase this one on it.",
   "issue": "`public import EpsilonEridani.Particles.Meson.Basic` makes inclusive DIS depend on the whole pseudoscalar-meson development (`PseudoscalarMeson`, `piPlus`/`kPlus`, `FlavorBreaking`) only for `LightFlavor` and `LightFlavor.charge` \u2014 the file uses nothing else from it (grep in this file yields exactly `open Particles.Meson (LightFlavor)` at line 87 and `open EpsilonEridani.Particles.Meson.LightFlavor` at line 173). `LightFlavor` is a quark-flavour type with quark charges, not meson theory; its home in `Meson/Basic.lean` is wrong, and this PR is the first consumer outside that module to pay for it.",
   "line": "8"
  }
 ],
